\section {Definitions}
      \subsection {Regularized Set}
      A set $S\subset \mathbb{R}^3$ is a regularized set $\iff S=\overline{int (S)}$.
      \subsection {Solid}
      Our goal is mainly focused on solids. A solid $S$ is defined as a regularized subset of $\mathbb{R}^3$  ($S\subset\mathbb{R}^3$)\\
      \subsection {Polyhedron}
      A polyhedron $P$ is the intersection of several half spaces. And the half spaces can be descirbed as a set $H=\{h_1,h_2,h_3,...h_n\}$\\

      A polyhedron $P$ contains features which can be described as three sets: a Vertex Set $V=\{v_1,v_2,...,v_m\}$ in which $v_i  (1\le i\le m)$ represents a vertex of the polyhedron $P$, $E=\{e_1,e_2,...,e_n\}$ in which $e_j  (1\le j\le n)$ represents an edge of $P$, $F=\{f_1,f_2,...,f_p\}$ in which $f_k  (1\le k\le p)$ represents a face of $P$.
